Every page primes its own translations (1.9.1)

Reported as: switch language, some pages are English, navigate away and
back and they are Persian again.

Root cause is not caching. On a client-side navigation Next re-renders
only the changed page segment and reuses the layout from the cached tree.
primeTranslations() lived only in the root layout, so it never ran for
those requests and t() returned the source Persian string. A hard load
was correct; navigating there was not — which is what made it look like
a cache problem.

All nineteen server pages prime translations themselves now. cache()
keeps it to one call per request.

Two supporting changes found while reproducing it:

- Sidebar links no longer prefetch. Every page is per-user — language,
  permissions, visible scope — so a prefetched copy is a copy of
  somebody's state at some earlier moment.
- Changing the language reloads the page. The router cache holds RSC
  payloads for routes already visited and neither revalidatePath nor
  router.refresh() clears them all. staleTimes cannot fix this either:
  Next rejects static below 30s and invalidates the whole block.

Also translates the theme label, which had never passed through t().

